    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d617">

                <pb facs="0599" n="515" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg515"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.48/385</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Garrett</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-10-18T13:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 18, 1917, 1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>729. Your 1487, October 15, 7 p.m. Not clear from your telegram whether German
                    Government has agreed to let Dutch Consul, Warsaw, control distribution of
                    American relief funds in general or only in the single case of $40,000
                    mentioned. Please explain.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
